<BaseLayout title="How we assess AI tools | AgentesVA" description="The sources, editorial criteria, and limitations behind the AgentesVA tool directory."><SiteHeader/><main id="main-content" class="en-page" data-pagefind-body><section class="en-hero"><div class="en-shell"><p class="en-kicker">Editorial methodology</p><h1 style="font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,68px);max-width:17ch;font-weight:550">How we assess AI tools.</h1><p class="en-lead">An editorial starting point for your own evaluation, based on research into public sources.</p></div></section><article class="en-section en-shell en-article"><h2>What the assessment represents</h2><p>The Spanish directory includes editorial scores out of five. These reflect our judgment of a tool’s fit for a small Spanish-speaking business. They are not controlled laboratory benchmarks, user ratings, or an objective measurement. Small differences should not be treated as decisive. English profiles focus on uses and getting started instead of reproducing scores.</p><h2>Where the information comes from</h2><ul><li>Official documentation and release notes.</li><li>Pricing pages and plan limits.</li><li>Public reviews on third-party platforms.</li><li>Specialist reporting and analysis.</li></ul><p>When a specific fact supports a comparison, the source is linked in the original article.</p><h2>What we consider</h2><ul><li>Fit for a small team without a dedicated technical department.</li><li>Value at entry level and how costs scale.</li><li>Effort needed to reach a useful first result.</li><li>Spanish-language support in the interface, documentation, and output.</li><li>Integrations and the ability to export data.</li><li>Product maturity and continuity.</li></ul><p>There is no fixed weighted formula. These factors inform an editorial judgment.</p><h2>Why scores cluster above four</h2><p>The directory is curated. Tools that do not meet the editorial threshold are generally not listed, so the distribution is not representative of the whole market. In the Spanish scale, 4.7–5.0 indicates a category reference, 4.3–4.6 a solid option with limitations, and 4.0–4.2 a useful niche tool with clearer tradeoffs.</p><h2>Commercial independence</h2><p>Some links are affiliate links. A purchase may generate a commission at no additional cost to the reader. Affiliate availability does not determine a score or position. We do not accept payment for a higher rating or inclusion. Sponsored content, if published, is identified in the article.</p><h2>Limitations and corrections</h2><p>Prices, features, and plans change. Editorial scores may lag behind product improvements or regressions. The directory covers broad business uses rather than every specialist industry. Verify the provider’s current offering before committing budget.</p><p>English editorial overviews are concise adaptations; full Spanish articles retain their original detail and reporting dates. If you find an error, contact <a href="mailto:hola@agentesva.com">hola@agentesva.com</a> with the tool or page and the correction needed.</p><a href="/tools/" class="en-button">Explore the tools</a></article></main><SiteFooter hideNewsletter/></BaseLayout>
